From: Artzig contributors
Subject: [PATCH] PermissionManagerService: select the hosted policy at startup

Reuse the original Binder facade, attribution registry and permission checker.
The hosted package registry supplies PermissionManagerServiceInterface before
startup instead of importing Android's legacy permission persistence stack.
Client classes and the service's permission/AppOps transactions are unchanged.

--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/pm/permission/PermissionManagerService.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/pm/permission/PermissionManagerService.java
@@ -162,9 +162,6 @@
 
-        if (PermissionManager.USE_ACCESS_CHECKING_SERVICE) {
-            mPermissionManagerServiceImpl = LocalServices.getService(
-                    PermissionManagerServiceInterface.class);
-        } else {
-            mPermissionManagerServiceImpl = new PermissionManagerServiceImpl(context,
-                    availableFeatures);
-        }
+        // Host adaptation: the session registers its package-backed permission policy.
+        // Android's legacy/access-checking stores require unavailable persistent state.
+        mPermissionManagerServiceImpl = Objects.requireNonNull(LocalServices.getService(
+                PermissionManagerServiceInterface.class), "Hosted permission policy not registered");
     }
